1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:04,000
They've been in use for over 3,000 years.

2
00:00:04,001 --> 00:00:07,000
But they're no longer only in physical space.

3
00:00:07,001 --> 00:00:09,000
They're in cyberspace as well.

4
00:00:09,001 --> 00:00:12,000
They're crafted with sophistication or simplicity.

5
00:00:12,001 --> 00:00:15,000
But make no mistake,

6
00:00:15,001 --> 00:00:19,000
using one today buys you a one-way ticket to the penitentiary.

7
00:00:19,001 --> 00:00:25,000
Now, Booby Traps on Modern Marvels.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,180
The explosion ripped through the mezzanine floor,

9
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:46,420
which houses the executive suites where the bomb was discovered early yesterday morning.

10
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:51,360
The FBI continued to keep this area around Krasinski's cabin cordoned off from the press.

11
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:56,800
They refused to deny or confirm reports that there was an explosion in this area earlier this morning.

12
00:00:56,801 --> 00:01:02,340
The elderly woman who opened the mailbox told her husband that the bomb looked like a flashlight.

13
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:04,640
It blew up when she touched it.

14
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:08,960
Each of these stories is a little different.

15
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:11,480
Yet each shares one thing in common.

16
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,960
The victims never saw it coming.

17
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:21,200
A booby trap is an explosive or mechanical trap that is designed to appear totally innocent.

18
00:01:21,201 --> 00:01:27,060
But when it's moved or touched by an unwary person, it suddenly goes off.

19
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:37,080
Anything at all can be booby-trapped, or booby-traps can be fabricated from just about anything that you can get your hands on.

20
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:39,920
Dynamite wired to a car's ignition.

21
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:44,960
As the key is turned, it ignites.

22
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,500
A shotgun hooked up to a doorknob.

23
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:50,000
When the door opens, it goes off.

24
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:58,460
Even a water faucet, rigged so when it's turned on, an entire house explodes.

25
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:02,840
Bottom line is, a lot of bad people out there with very vivid imagination.

26
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:08,620
Most booby traps are meant to kill or seriously injure their intended victims.

27
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:18,500
Others are designed to harass and intimidate.

28
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:22,320
But whatever their purpose, they're showing up more and more,

29
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:24,920
not only on faraway battlefields,

30
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:29,680
but on our streets and in our workplaces, even in our homes.

31
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,620
The motives are almost endless.

32
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:36,180
Revenge, love triangles, property protection,

33
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:42,620
homicide, extortion, drug dealing, you name it, it runs the gamut.

34
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:46,420
According to the latest figures from the FBI

35
00:02:46,421 --> 00:02:50,060
in the U.S. Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, and Firearms, or ATF.

36
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,360
There's been a record number of bombings or attempted bombings

37
00:02:53,361 --> 00:02:55,900
recorded in the United States since 1993.

38
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:59,080
That number exceeded 8,000.

39
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:02,900
Ten to 15% were directly related to booby trap incidents.

40
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:05,260
That number is expected to increase.

41
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:10,280
I believe the use of booby traps in the future

42
00:03:10,281 --> 00:03:12,580
is going to continue to come on.

43
00:03:12,581 --> 00:03:17,900
There are so many ways that you can devise a booby trap around technology.

44
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:26,560
The fact that there is such easy access to information detailing the ins and outs of booby trap construction isn't helping.

45
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:32,540
There's a lot of publications and manuals out there put out by various government agencies

46
00:03:32,541 --> 00:03:37,860
as well as clandestine type publications that give that type of information.

47
00:03:37,861 --> 00:03:43,260
but without a doubt the internet is probably one of the largest information sources we see

48
00:03:43,261 --> 00:03:48,080
when people are experimenting or making explosive devices, kids especially.

49
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:54,100
In the make-believe world of video games and action movies,

50
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:56,360
booby traps are edge-of-the-seat thrillers.

51
00:03:57,420 --> 00:04:02,600
Audiences are delighted with the unique devices set up to protect the mummified remains of an Egyptian pharaoh

52
00:04:02,601 --> 00:04:05,800
and the rich treasures hidden alongside his corpse.

53
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:14,860
In reality, the ancient Egyptians used booby traps sparingly.

54
00:04:14,861 --> 00:04:20,860
The pharaoh's builders camouflaged the entrances to their tombs with rocks and debris

55
00:04:20,861 --> 00:04:25,860
and carved curses into the entrances and on the walls inside the tomb.

56
00:04:25,861 --> 00:04:31,860
They would do things like have a meandering pattern for the corridors.

57
00:04:31,861 --> 00:04:35,860
Sometimes some of them would end in false chambers.

58
00:04:35,861 --> 00:04:41,525
chambers. Some of them would be dead ends. Some of them would double back.

59
00:04:41,526 --> 00:04:42,520
Some of these

60
00:04:42,521 --> 00:04:48,920
corridors were blocked with huge stones that slid into place when the tomb was sealed.

61
00:04:48,921 --> 00:04:55,700
But for a select number of tombs, ancient engineers employed several ingenious devices

62
00:04:55,701 --> 00:04:58,540
to send a crystal clear message to the would-be grave robber.

63
00:04:58,541 --> 00:05:05,540
One of the obvious ways of making a booby trap would be to have rocks fall on someone.

64
00:05:05,541 --> 00:05:10,540
And even though the Egyptians didn't do that very often, we do have a couple of examples of it occurring.

65
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:16,540
A popular trap was the man-burying booby trap.

66
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:22,540
A large funnel was hollowed out in the ceiling of the corridor that led to the burial chamber.

67
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:26,540
The funnel was then filled with rocks and sand.

68
00:05:26,541 --> 00:05:30,540
A large blocking stone was then rolled in under the shaft.

69
00:05:30,541 --> 00:05:36,540
A robber trying to dig around the blocking stone would trigger the sticks holding the

70
00:05:36,541 --> 00:05:40,540
funnel together, collapsing the entire thing and burying the thief alive.

71
00:05:40,541 --> 00:05:47,540
In the tomb that we were working on a few years ago, we ran across exactly the same

72
00:05:47,541 --> 00:05:53,540
thing and the remnants of that funnel actually did come down at one point and we had to evacuate

73
00:05:53,541 --> 00:05:55,540
the tomb very, very quickly.

74
00:05:56,540 --> 00:06:02,480
Tomb builders also liked digging bottomless pits hidden under camouflaged covers.

75
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:10,920
A single careless step would send unsuspecting intruders plummeting through a false floor and into a dark abyss.

76
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:17,280
The deeper ones of these, of course, they would never be able to scale their way out of.

77
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:23,520
There's some evidence that suggests poisonous powders were spread across the burial chamber's floor.

78
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:29,540
When an intruder entered, the powders were released into the air and inhaled.

79
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:37,560
In fact, a poisonous substance was unleashed in a tomb in Egypt's Valley of the Golden Mummies in September 2000,

80
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:43,240
as archaeologist Zahi Hawass and his team entered the main burial chamber.

81
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:49,340
Without realizing it, they stepped into a two-foot layer of yellow powder, sending it airborne.

82
00:06:49,341 --> 00:06:56,340
The team became ill almost instantly and was forced to evacuate.

83
00:06:56,341 --> 00:07:01,340
Twenty workers wearing gas masks labored for two weeks to remove the mysterious substance,

84
00:07:01,341 --> 00:07:04,340
later identified as tainted iron oxide.

85
00:07:04,341 --> 00:07:06,340
But was it a booby trap?

86
00:07:06,341 --> 00:07:14,340
The only question, of course, is whether this material was put there by the Egyptians.

87
00:07:14,341 --> 00:07:21,800
There is indication that in some of the tombs there is lethal bacteria and molds that have come on the walls.

88
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:24,500
Aspergillus is one of them that has been recognized.

89
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:35,760
Over 4,000 miles east of Egypt's Valley of the Golden Mummies lay the ruins of one of the greatest discoveries of all time.

90
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:40,980
It is here that archaeologists struggle with a far more deadly puzzle.

91
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:52,960
100,000 slaves toiled for 36 years to build the mausoleum of the Chinese emperor, Qin Shi Huang.

92
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:57,740
It covered 10 square miles and was buried 15 stories underground.

93
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:06,540
For two millennia, an army of 8,000 life-sized terracotta soldiers and horses kept watch over his complex burial site.

94
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:12,080
According to folklore, scores of booby traps wait in silence as well.

95
00:08:12,081 --> 00:08:15,760
by popular myth and legend.

96
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,880
The tomb is protected by an elaborate system

97
00:08:18,881 --> 00:08:21,900
of crossbows and other weapons

98
00:08:21,901 --> 00:08:26,540
waiting to be discharged at any potential grave robber.

99
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:29,160
There are also supposed to be large ponds

100
00:08:29,161 --> 00:08:33,340
or even rivers of mercury placed inside the tomb

101
00:08:33,341 --> 00:08:35,980
for its noxious fumes,

102
00:08:35,981 --> 00:08:39,940
which would theoretically overcome any intruder.

103
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,660
Today, most of the site has yet to be excavated.

104
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:51,020
One of the reasons is that Chinese archaeologists and their workers believe that crossbows do exist.

105
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:55,280
They are proceeding slowly with great caution,

106
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:59,960
so as not to become modern victims of the Chinese emperor's ancient booby traps.

107
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:09,280
Early engineers had managed to turn the art of protecting burial grounds and tombs into a deadly science.

108
00:09:09,281 --> 00:09:18,860
But it would take ancient armies and military geniuses to transform booby traps from guardians of the dead to weapons of war.

109
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:27,220
The term booby trap originated in the mid-1800s and defined a type of practical joke.

110
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:33,020
It required a gullible victim, the booby, who could be fooled into getting caught in some kind of comical trap.

111
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:36,080
Booby traps will continue on Modern Marvels.

112
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:43,380
It was on the battlefields of North Africa, Greece, and the ancient Near East

113
00:09:43,381 --> 00:09:47,600
that military geniuses like Alexander the Great and Julius Caesar

114
00:09:47,601 --> 00:09:50,820
first discovered the tactical significance of booby traps.

115
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:55,260
By setting up hidden snares and traps,

116
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:58,600
they realized they could injure or kill unsuspecting enemies

117
00:09:58,601 --> 00:10:00,800
without exposing their own troops to danger.

118
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:06,260
Early on, commanders favored camouflaged pits,

119
00:10:06,261 --> 00:10:08,660
deep enough to hold razor-sharp spears

120
00:10:08,661 --> 00:10:10,540
angled to impale the foe.

121
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:13,640
The other thing was a cauldrop,

122
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:16,740
which was a sharpened triangular piece of metal

123
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:18,740
that could be thrown out in front

124
00:10:18,741 --> 00:10:22,300
so that the enemy would run over it with their horses,

125
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,720
but it could also be used as an anti-infantry weapon.

126
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,940
Julius Caesar used cauldrops

127
00:10:27,941 --> 00:10:30,440
during the Battle of Alicia in 52 B.C.

128
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,940
As his legions seemed headed for defeat,

129
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:39,420
Caesar ordered hundreds of caltrips to be strategically positioned on the ground in front of his defenses.

130
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:44,140
As wave after wave of the Gallic cavalry charged his line,

131
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:49,840
his hidden booby traps tore at the hooves of the attacking army's horses, slowing down their assault.

132
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:57,760
Military historians believe it was this strategy that helped Julius Caesar to turn a losing battle into a victory.

133
00:10:57,761 --> 00:11:04,660
not surprisingly today there is a modern version of the ancient cauldron

134
00:11:04,661 --> 00:11:10,140
the road spikes used by police officers in pursuit of a suspect fleeing in a vehicle

135
00:11:10,141 --> 00:11:17,920
the spikes are made in a certain way that they'll always be upright and when the bad

136
00:11:17,921 --> 00:11:21,220
guy runs over it and flattens all four tires and hopefully stops the pursuit

137
00:11:21,221 --> 00:11:29,460
The invention of gunpowder in Asia during the 12th century vastly increased the potential

138
00:11:29,461 --> 00:11:32,460
for carnage on the battlefield.

139
00:11:32,461 --> 00:11:39,920
As a result, gunpowder soon became a staple ingredient in the manufacture of booby traps.

140
00:11:39,921 --> 00:11:44,000
In Europe during the Middle Ages, warring kings and landowners protected the length

141
00:11:44,001 --> 00:11:48,360
and breadth of their estates' boundaries by laying tripwires connected to containers

142
00:11:48,361 --> 00:11:51,340
packed with explosives, nails, and broken glass.

143
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:55,720
During the American Civil War,

144
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:58,780
it was soldiers on both sides who took booby-trapping

145
00:11:58,781 --> 00:12:00,520
to a new level of sophistication.

146
00:12:01,340 --> 00:12:03,460
We have a pistol barrel,

147
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:07,520
a lock work off a regular percussion-type weapon system,

148
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:08,440
and a trigger.

149
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:10,800
And as the triggering mechanism is disturbed,

150
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,260
the safety bar would fall free,

151
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,660
the locking mechanism would trip forward,

152
00:12:14,661 --> 00:12:16,300
and bang, they have their man.

153
00:12:16,301 --> 00:12:23,300
They connected their devices to everyday objects like a spoon or a jackknife.

154
00:12:23,301 --> 00:12:26,300
The items were left behind when they moved out of the area.

155
00:12:26,301 --> 00:12:29,300
The booby traps were literally hidden in plain sight.

156
00:12:29,301 --> 00:12:34,300
When the enemy entered the abandoned camp and picked up the harmless looking spoon or knife,

157
00:12:34,301 --> 00:12:37,300
the booby trap would detonate.

158
00:12:37,301 --> 00:12:44,300
By the time World War I began in 1914, the machine gun and artillery were the dominant

159
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:53,435
weapons on the battlefield. The use of this hardware made free movement impossible.

160
00:12:53,436 --> 00:12:54,136
So

161
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:57,471
both sides adopted trench warfare.

162
00:12:57,472 --> 00:13:00,980
But as the American, French and British forces attempted

163
00:13:00,981 --> 00:13:06,775
to storm the German trenches, they found that yet another deadly weapon awaited them.

164
00:13:06,776 --> 00:13:07,476
The

165
00:13:07,477 --> 00:13:10,500
The Germans got very good at booby-trapping devices,

166
00:13:10,780 --> 00:13:13,540
like tripwires across the entrances of dugouts,

167
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:17,180
so that if you entered a dugout and you'd hit the tripwire, it would explode.

168
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:21,940
They also got very good at booby-trapping a helmet or a Luger pistol,

169
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:23,660
because everybody wants a souvenir.

170
00:13:24,380 --> 00:13:28,940
So these things were rigged in such a way that if you moved them, they would explode.

171
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:35,480
During World War II, the art and science of the military booby-trap exploded.

172
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:37,540
literally and figuratively.

173
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:44,640
There is a combination of ways that a booby trap can be triggered.

174
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:51,700
One way is pressure, and then any pressure on this would crush the exploder,

175
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,180
and it would go off.

176
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:56,140
You could also rig this up as a trip wire,

177
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:59,340
so that when you pull this, it would go off.

178
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:02,100
You could make this also a tension release device,

179
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:05,360
so that if you cut the wire, it would also go off.

180
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:13,020
German soldiers planted booby traps along roads and in fields to catch the unsuspecting or the inquisitive.

181
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:23,600
Allied soldiers landing on the beaches of Normandy on D-Day met anti-tank barriers that were rigged to explode if moved.

182
00:14:23,601 --> 00:14:33,920
as the allies pushed farther inland they found that the germans had laid tripwires attached to

183
00:14:33,921 --> 00:14:39,280
explosives across doorways and staircases or attached to doors cupboards and windows

184
00:14:39,281 --> 00:14:45,580
soldiers don't go through doors they go through the windows and you'd smash a window in with your

185
00:14:45,581 --> 00:14:49,360
rifle butt. And when you smashed it, you were going to set the explosive ball.

186
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:58,320
In late 1944, during their drive across northwestern Europe, Allied forces came across an abandoned

187
00:14:58,321 --> 00:14:59,744
German headquarters.

188
00:14:59,745 --> 00:15:04,800
No mines or booby traps were found, but when a soldier urinated against

189
00:15:04,801 --> 00:15:09,800
the building wall, an electrical connection made by the urine set off a booby trap that

190
00:15:09,801 --> 00:15:10,800
destroyed that building.

191
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:18,380
The Japanese planted a substantial number of booby traps against the Allies, using them

192
00:15:18,381 --> 00:15:23,620
in the jungles, along beaches, anywhere they figured they could fool an unsuspecting or

193
00:15:23,621 --> 00:15:24,400
curious GI.

194
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:31,600
They often booby-trapped desirable objects such as food and sake, or war souvenirs like

195
00:15:31,601 --> 00:15:32,580
rifles and helmets.

196
00:15:32,581 --> 00:15:36,620
desperate to get in the last punch

197
00:15:36,621 --> 00:15:40,820
they even booby trapped the bodies of their own dead or wounded soldiers

198
00:15:40,821 --> 00:15:47,260
you did not want to disturb a japanese body in world war ii

199
00:15:47,261 --> 00:15:52,020
there was the pressure to release device where if you move the body the pressure would be

200
00:15:52,021 --> 00:15:55,080
released and an explosive device would go off

201
00:15:55,081 --> 00:16:00,700
but the use of booby traps on the american side was limited

202
00:16:00,701 --> 00:16:08,020
Amazingly, it took permission from a three-star general for an American soldier to set up a trap.

203
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:17,560
During the Indochina Wars, it was the Viet Cong who were unmatched for ingenuity and deadly effectiveness with booby traps.

204
00:16:20,820 --> 00:16:24,000
They improvised mines out of any explosives they could find,

205
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:27,240
packing them into seemingly harmless objects.

206
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:30,340
Fruit hanging from a tree.

207
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:34,660
a pile of buffalo dung, even an empty ginger jar.

208
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:40,120
When I was in Vietnam, the most common booby trap that we ran into

209
00:16:40,121 --> 00:16:43,280
was nothing more than a tin can with a hand grenade stuck in there

210
00:16:43,281 --> 00:16:45,720
with a trip wire across the trail.

211
00:16:46,180 --> 00:16:47,820
You'd come along, you'd trip the wire,

212
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:51,380
you'd pull the hand grenade out of the tin can,

213
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:53,300
and it would explode.

214
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:59,260
A centuries-old favorite of the Viet Cong was the punji pit.

215
00:16:59,261 --> 00:17:01,760
various size pits were dug

216
00:17:01,761 --> 00:17:04,100
sharpened bamboo was then planted upward

217
00:17:04,101 --> 00:17:05,080
at the bottom of the pit

218
00:17:05,081 --> 00:17:08,300
most were just large enough to impale

219
00:17:08,301 --> 00:17:09,100
a victim's foot

220
00:17:09,101 --> 00:17:12,480
a few were big enough to swallow a man

221
00:17:12,481 --> 00:17:16,420
another ingeniously arranged trap

222
00:17:16,421 --> 00:17:17,500
was the bamboo whip

223
00:17:17,501 --> 00:17:20,340
a green bamboo pole with spikes

224
00:17:20,341 --> 00:17:22,140
attached to an end was pulled back

225
00:17:22,141 --> 00:17:23,600
and held by a catch device

226
00:17:23,601 --> 00:17:26,140
when the trip wire

227
00:17:26,141 --> 00:17:27,960
stretched across the trail was triggered

228
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:32,160
The whip would snap back, impaling whoever set it off.

229
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:38,940
In the 1990s, during the civil wars throughout Bosnia, Croatia, and Kosovo,

230
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:43,480
the Serbs made extensive use of indiscriminate mine laying and booby-trapping.

231
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:50,200
Their intention was to terrorize and thereby control the civilian population.

232
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:57,180
Booby-trapped mines were placed in residential rubble to prevent anyone from rebuilding a house.

233
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:04,580
The booby traps were rigged to everyday objects in and around houses and farms.

234
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:07,580
Doors, light switches, even televisions.

235
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:11,320
Grenades were typically employed as booby traps.

236
00:18:11,321 --> 00:18:14,460
They would remove the pin and the safety from a hand grenade,

237
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:17,520
and they would slip it into a glass or a jar,

238
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,780
something that would hold the spoon in place.

239
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:23,060
And then they would place it very precariously on a door handle.

240
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:26,920
When you would have someone walk into a room and they would turn the door handle,

241
00:18:26,921 --> 00:18:32,060
the glass would fall and break, and then the grenade detonates as the person is walking into the room.

242
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:42,640
One very complex booby trap consisted of a pile of explosives hidden in the attic of a house,

243
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:46,360
then linked by an elaborate wiring system to the kitchen faucet.

244
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:51,100
Anyone who turned on the tap for a drink of water would close the electric circuit,

245
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:53,480
setting off a fatal explosion.

246
00:18:56,920 --> 00:19:01,860
But soon, booby-trapping would reach a whole new level of destruction,

247
00:19:02,700 --> 00:19:06,840
turning an entire town into a single, massive trap.

248
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:14,920
Approximately 10% of the American casualties in Vietnam were caused by booby-traps.

249
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:19,320
Among those injured was Captain Colin Powell, who later became Secretary of State.

250
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:22,080
Booby-Trap will continue on Modern Marvels.

251
00:19:22,081 --> 00:19:32,180
It was dawn when the Israeli army entered the Palestinian town of Janine in the nearby refugee camp in March 2002.

252
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:35,720
What they found shocked them.

253
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:41,440
More booby traps per square inch than had ever been discovered in one location.

254
00:19:42,060 --> 00:19:47,720
Some of the booby trapped bombs were huge, containing as much as 250 pounds of explosives.

255
00:19:47,721 --> 00:19:54,720
Compare this with a typical suicide bomber, whose explosive content is a mere 25 pounds.

256
00:19:54,721 --> 00:20:02,720
Israeli bulldozers rolled along the principal roads leading into Janine, clearing booby traps along the way.

257
00:20:02,721 --> 00:20:09,720
In one three-quarter mile stretch of road, 124 separate booby traps were found and detonated.

258
00:20:09,721 --> 00:20:15,720
In the refugee camp, the explosive charges were even more densely packed.

259
00:20:15,721 --> 00:20:16,421
Pact.

260
00:20:16,422 --> 00:20:24,200
Over three days, 23 Israeli soldiers and 52 Palestinians were killed, many by rubble

261
00:20:24,201 --> 00:20:28,420
from the exploding booby traps and mines with which Palestinian fighters had honeycombed

262
00:20:28,421 --> 00:20:32,600
the camp. Some of the bombs they found were landmines.

263
00:20:32,601 --> 00:20:35,000
Others were landmines made into

264
00:20:35,001 --> 00:20:35,701
booby traps.

265
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:43,560
Improvising a mine for the explosive content is really good because you have a large explosive

266
00:20:43,561 --> 00:20:45,820
ready to go right there.

267
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:50,240
The mechanical differences between booby traps and landmines are few.

268
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:55,280
Both use the same type of firing devices and explosive-laden containers.

269
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,660
The differences are in their purpose.

270
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:02,680
Landmines are designed to be positioned solely in the ground.

271
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:05,380
In this way, they serve their primary purpose,

272
00:21:05,780 --> 00:21:07,440
to slow down an enemy's advance.

273
00:21:07,441 --> 00:21:18,200
a booby trap however can be anywhere and it is usually disguised to look like an innocent object

274
00:21:18,201 --> 00:21:23,300
even as a soldier successfully scans the ground for landmines

275
00:21:23,301 --> 00:21:28,900
the possibility of detonating a booby trap exists everywhere all around him

276
00:21:28,901 --> 00:21:36,660
it is a constant relentless unforgiving threat in this way the booby trap serves its purpose

277
00:21:36,661 --> 00:21:40,680
to create doubt by amping up the stress level.

278
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:45,740
A booby trap makes its money on catching the enemy unaware.

279
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:54,000
It really has that psychological impact on his morale.

280
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:59,300
The fact that booby traps are so hard to detect

281
00:21:59,301 --> 00:22:02,360
makes them a truly sinister tool of destruction and terror.

282
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:12,160
American forces in Afghanistan were in constant danger of detonating booby traps.

283
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:18,300
Most Al-Qaeda caves or weapons cache sites were loaded with them.

284
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:22,480
When a soldier or a Marine did find a booby trap,

285
00:22:23,540 --> 00:22:29,160
his standing order was to let the Explosive Ordnance Disposal, or EOD, personnel deal with it.

286
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:34,780
The reason the EOD people went in to try to take care of that

287
00:22:34,781 --> 00:22:39,200
was there was a possibility that there were also documents in there,

288
00:22:39,420 --> 00:22:44,300
anything that could be used as evidence and possible indicators

289
00:22:44,301 --> 00:22:49,040
as to what al-Qaeda might do then and in the future.

290
00:22:50,620 --> 00:22:53,660
Once a cave had been cleared, it was demolished.

291
00:22:57,220 --> 00:22:59,940
Today we're going to talk about some mines that can be booby-trapped,

292
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,060
manufactured in Yugoslavia.

293
00:23:02,061 --> 00:23:05,840
This group is currently being trained to detect a variety of the latest booby traps.

294
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:12,640
Those manufactured by the military and those that are improvised by terrorists and guerrillas.

295
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:17,900
The way it's used as a booby trap is going to be a trip wire or a pressure function.

296
00:23:18,460 --> 00:23:23,360
We teach Marines that there exists the possibility that every obstacle is booby trapped.

297
00:23:23,980 --> 00:23:25,320
Sir, not as more. Hand me that mine.

298
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:34,200
It's that easy to go home in a plastic bag.

299
00:23:34,201 --> 00:23:38,280
Notice I didn't say a body bag, a plastic bag. That's all that's going to be left.

300
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:46,920
How they handle a booby trap depends largely upon how much damage they can accept in the vicinity of the trap.

301
00:23:49,160 --> 00:23:57,879
If damage is unacceptable, for example, if you're working in the building, mark the booby trap and request some assistance from explosive ordnance disposal personnel

302
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:59,200
or some combat engineers.

303
00:23:59,201 --> 00:24:03,740
If you can accept a certain degree of damage to the area that you're operating in,

304
00:24:03,820 --> 00:24:07,200
the preferred method is to detonate the booby trap in place.

305
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:15,640
To help ensure their safety, the Marine EOD personnel often rely on tools,

306
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:18,580
like this remotely controlled robot called Andros.

307
00:24:20,300 --> 00:24:26,140
We can use it to recon the suspect item, and if it is a bomb or booby trap,

308
00:24:26,141 --> 00:24:31,300
We can use this device also to disarm or disrupt or even x-ray or move the device.

309
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,720
I've got three different video cameras on board.

310
00:24:34,620 --> 00:24:36,260
This is my forward-looking camera.

311
00:24:37,360 --> 00:24:39,080
And this is a side-view camera.

312
00:24:39,580 --> 00:24:42,160
It has pan, tilt, and zoom features in it.

313
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:44,560
This is my bottom-view camera.

314
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:48,120
It's got all the basic features of a regular arm.

315
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:50,360
It's got a shoulder, a wrist, an elbow.

316
00:24:51,420 --> 00:24:53,560
It's got a gripper that acts like a hand.

317
00:24:53,660 --> 00:24:55,480
I can open and close the gripper.

318
00:24:56,140 --> 00:24:58,220
The wrist turns 360 degrees.

319
00:24:58,940 --> 00:25:05,480
As long as I can reach it, which usually is about 7 feet, I can do anything I want with it.

320
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:14,400
But remote control robots like Andros were not available to military EOD during the war in Somalia in 1993.

321
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:20,600
Disarming the improvised booby traps had to be done carefully, the old-fashioned way.

322
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:25,240
In Somalia, we encountered booby traps almost on a daily basis.

323
00:25:25,241 --> 00:25:31,020
They would use very simple booby traps, things like hand grenades under rocks,

324
00:25:31,500 --> 00:25:34,420
hand grenades wedged between doorways.

325
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:41,160
Somalian warlords and their hired thugs seldom used booby traps in a military sense.

326
00:25:41,680 --> 00:25:46,040
They did use them to terrorize and then to extort money from their own countrymen.

327
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:49,260
There were two or three well stations in the city.

328
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:52,840
People would take a landmine, put a hand grenade underneath of it,

329
00:25:52,841 --> 00:25:56,680
and they'd make it readily obvious that you could see it.

330
00:25:58,460 --> 00:26:02,220
The warlords created visible booby-trapped mazes around the wells,

331
00:26:02,580 --> 00:26:06,360
then stood with their guns poised and their open hands outstretched,

332
00:26:06,940 --> 00:26:11,360
ready to take payment for leading thirsty Somalis safely through the maze to the well.

333
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:16,180
We would work on a daily basis to go out and clear some of these booby-trapped items.

334
00:26:17,460 --> 00:26:20,800
Extortion isn't the only motive for the bad guys setting booby traps.

335
00:26:20,801 --> 00:26:25,460
Some of the most famous mad bombers were just that.

336
00:26:26,980 --> 00:26:27,680
Mad Men.

337
00:26:29,880 --> 00:26:38,460
Around the world, someone is killed or injured by a booby trap, landmine, or other similar explosive device every 22 minutes.

338
00:26:39,300 --> 00:26:41,700
Booby traps will continue on Modern Marvels.

339
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:49,600
New York City in the mid-20th century.

340
00:26:49,601 --> 00:26:53,720
world famous for its fast pace, sophistication and glamour

341
00:26:53,721 --> 00:26:56,120
but lurking just beneath the surface

342
00:26:56,121 --> 00:26:58,120
there was a feeling of uneasiness

343
00:26:58,121 --> 00:27:01,520
for 16 years

344
00:27:01,521 --> 00:27:06,000
an anonymous crackpot secretly planted booby traps in public places

345
00:27:06,001 --> 00:27:08,740
New Yorkers nervously referred to him

346
00:27:08,741 --> 00:27:10,680
as the Mad Bomber

347
00:27:10,681 --> 00:27:14,960
he planted 32 bombs in all

348
00:27:14,961 --> 00:27:17,480
from 1940 until 1956

349
00:27:17,481 --> 00:27:21,980
One was attached to a seat in a movie theater.

350
00:27:23,620 --> 00:27:26,360
22 people were wounded, many critically.

351
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:31,940
The bomber's anger appeared to be directed at the city's power company,

352
00:27:32,580 --> 00:27:34,280
to which he sent a letter that read,

353
00:27:35,260 --> 00:27:37,300
I can make the Con Edison sorry.

354
00:27:38,260 --> 00:27:40,420
When we look at profiles of bombers,

355
00:27:40,680 --> 00:27:43,860
normally we're looking at someone who is angry,

356
00:27:43,861 --> 00:27:46,280
but it's also someone who is focused.

357
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:52,660
The bomb itself gives him an outlet for his anger, for his frustration,

358
00:27:52,980 --> 00:27:57,120
and it gives him the ability to strike out at society.

359
00:27:59,500 --> 00:28:03,340
The serial bomber turned out to be a polite, well-dressed, but delusional fellow

360
00:28:03,341 --> 00:28:04,780
by the name of George Metesky.

361
00:28:08,220 --> 00:28:11,560
Metesky built his booby traps in the garage of the apartment he shared

362
00:28:11,561 --> 00:28:14,460
with his two unmarried sisters in Waterbury, Connecticut.

363
00:28:14,461 --> 00:28:20,460
His bombs were handmade, out of corrugated pipe, gunpowder, and a trigger mechanism.

364
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:29,060
Ted Kaczynski, the man known as the Unabomber, may have been inspired by New York's mad bomber.

365
00:28:29,900 --> 00:28:34,940
On some level, he was probably impacted by Metesky and other bombers

366
00:28:34,941 --> 00:28:42,180
and developed his deadly activities along the same lines that had happened nearly half a century before.

367
00:28:42,181 --> 00:28:48,900
Kaczynski had a gripe against anyone he believed was corrupting the environment with modern technology.

368
00:28:50,340 --> 00:28:54,380
Among his targets were airlines, universities, and manufacturers.

369
00:28:54,840 --> 00:29:00,880
This was a case that ran approximately 18 years with a series of bombings all across the United States.

370
00:29:02,260 --> 00:29:05,800
Kaczynski was able to stay one step ahead of his relentless pursuers,

371
00:29:06,260 --> 00:29:09,940
because like George Metesky, his booby traps also were handmade.

372
00:29:12,180 --> 00:29:15,040
In an isolated cabin in Montana with no electricity,

373
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:21,160
Kaczynski carefully crafted his bomb parts from pieces of mahogany and other hardwoods used in furniture.

374
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:25,500
One bomb contained a twig from a cherry tree.

375
00:29:26,320 --> 00:29:31,860
Even the screws that were used to put it together, he had crafted from hand.

376
00:29:32,300 --> 00:29:35,260
They were a labor of absolute love for him.

377
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:41,960
Three people who opened Kaczynski's plain-wrapped, homemade wooden boxes were killed.

378
00:29:42,180 --> 00:29:44,940
Another 23 were wounded.

379
00:29:48,420 --> 00:29:54,620
The victims of the most recent serial bomber were ordinary citizens living the quiet life in America's heartland.

380
00:29:56,280 --> 00:29:59,760
Their terror lasted for one week in May 2002.

381
00:30:00,800 --> 00:30:05,640
The scare started on Friday when eight pipe bombs were found in Illinois and eastern Iowa.

382
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:11,020
The FBI says six people were hurt by those bombs, including four postal workers.

383
00:30:11,021 --> 00:30:15,420
You think out here in a rural Nebraska, it's not going to happen.

384
00:30:15,620 --> 00:30:18,840
Why they picked our road, I have no idea.

385
00:30:19,600 --> 00:30:24,460
One more time, it appeared to be random bombings without purpose,

386
00:30:24,860 --> 00:30:30,780
and the authorities were forced to consider anything from members of militia groups

387
00:30:30,781 --> 00:30:36,200
to international terrorists to high school kids with bombs.

388
00:30:36,201 --> 00:30:44,980
A nationwide manhunt resulted in the arrest of Luke Helder, a 21-year-old industrial design student.

389
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:51,640
He said he planted booby traps because he didn't like the way the government created laws that he felt manipulated lives.

390
00:30:52,960 --> 00:30:56,160
Buying the parts to put his booby traps together was easy.

391
00:30:56,640 --> 00:31:05,160
Luke Helder, like so many other makers of booby traps, was able to purchase all of the components for his deadly devices,

392
00:31:05,161 --> 00:31:10,820
devices simply by going to local stores and purchasing over-the-counter the supplies,

393
00:31:11,020 --> 00:31:15,260
the equipment that he needed. There was no license. There was no identity check.

394
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:21,920
He told authorities the placement of the bombs in mailboxes across the country was to create

395
00:31:21,921 --> 00:31:24,563
a smiley face on the U.S. map.

396
00:31:24,564 --> 00:31:29,320
Reports of booby traps killing or injuring victims has

397
00:31:29,321 --> 00:31:32,470
increased 60 percent over the past decade.

398
00:31:32,471 --> 00:31:35,620
Surprisingly, most were guarding pot farms

399
00:31:35,621 --> 00:31:39,161
or meth labs from thieves and police.

400
00:31:39,162 --> 00:31:43,660
Many marijuana farms, especially in the western

401
00:31:43,661 --> 00:31:46,380
U.S., rely on well-placed booby traps for protection.

402
00:31:46,900 --> 00:31:50,980
One of the most common and more deadly booby traps that we find around marijuana patches

403
00:31:50,981 --> 00:31:52,649
is the shotgun-type trap.

404
00:31:52,650 --> 00:31:56,720
It's made out of a Kutman rat trap, wood, and a three-quarter

405
00:31:56,721 --> 00:31:58,489
inch diameter plumbing pipe.

406
00:31:58,490 --> 00:32:02,280
What the booby trapper does is insert the shotgun shell into

407
00:32:02,281 --> 00:32:08,500
the plumbing pipe, finds a suitable support like a stump, attaches the wood to the stump,

408
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:10,196
brings the bale around.

409
00:32:10,197 --> 00:32:13,900
The unsuspecting officer comes down the trail, hits the wire,

410
00:32:14,980 --> 00:32:18,620
causes the pin to slip out, and it fires the device.

411
00:32:18,621 --> 00:32:21,280
Less deadly but exceptionally painful.

412
00:32:21,520 --> 00:32:26,360
Are booby traps designed to harass law enforcement or intimidate thieves wanting

413
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:27,700
to steal the marijuana plants.

414
00:32:29,360 --> 00:32:33,800
One thing we'll typically see is either single or double-edged razor blades,

415
00:32:34,140 --> 00:32:38,160
which are placed down in the stock of a marijuana plant.

416
00:32:38,600 --> 00:32:42,380
It deters people from just reaching in and grabbing the plant and pulling it out

417
00:32:42,381 --> 00:32:44,520
because they're going to get cut if they don't know it's there.

418
00:32:45,820 --> 00:32:49,780
There's another painful non-lethal trap out there that tears at the face.

419
00:32:51,080 --> 00:32:55,080
It's just a simple fish hook with fishing line attached to it.

420
00:32:55,081 --> 00:32:58,580
You can see it's very, very sharp on the end and has barbs.

421
00:32:59,120 --> 00:33:03,060
Where we'll typically find these is hanging on small branches.

422
00:33:04,860 --> 00:33:09,540
When you walk through here, they're going to either snag in your eye, in your cheek, your scalp,

423
00:33:09,700 --> 00:33:12,060
or somewhere along in your head area.

424
00:33:12,560 --> 00:33:14,920
And with the barbs on them, they're not going to come out very easily.

425
00:33:17,620 --> 00:33:21,240
Meth labs rigged with booby traps present another deadly challenge.

426
00:33:21,241 --> 00:33:30,060
More than 18 law enforcement officers were killed and hundreds of others wounded in recent years, attempting to enter and close down these illicit operations.

427
00:33:30,061 --> 00:33:35,720
We have found shotgun booby traps behind doors where you open the door and it fires a shotgun.

428
00:33:36,220 --> 00:33:45,360
They're also finding a lot of chemical type booby traps, probably not going to kill them, but could seriously injure them and cause potential long-term damage.

429
00:33:46,120 --> 00:33:50,900
Not all booby traps are meant to kill or injure. Some are to provide early warning.

430
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:56,680
A very simple device is nothing more than a trip wire, empty can, handful of pebbles.

431
00:33:57,340 --> 00:34:03,900
Pebbles go in the can, officer comes down a trail, it'll disturb the wire, causes a rattling sound,

432
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:07,580
gives the pot farmers down the road an opportunity to get away.

433
00:34:09,580 --> 00:34:13,880
Experts agree that the chances are slim for the average citizen to be caught by a booby trap.

434
00:34:16,080 --> 00:34:18,760
But these same experts caution that it is possible,

435
00:34:18,761 --> 00:34:26,660
especially for hikers or bicyclists who innocently wander into a marijuana field on public lands.

436
00:34:28,620 --> 00:34:31,880
If you're in a national forest, if you're in a state park,

437
00:34:32,480 --> 00:34:36,760
there's the possibility that you could stumble onto an illegal marijuana grow

438
00:34:36,761 --> 00:34:41,420
that is booby-trapped with either lethal or non-lethal means, or both.

439
00:34:41,421 --> 00:34:50,400
One very famous booby trap case involved a gambling casino in a small Nevada town called Stateline.

440
00:34:51,260 --> 00:34:52,480
The year was 1981.

441
00:34:53,380 --> 00:34:55,820
They made this big bomb, they put it in the Harvey's Casino,

442
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:58,920
they said, you give us some money and we'll tell you how to take it apart.

443
00:34:59,160 --> 00:35:00,440
Classic extortion bombing.

444
00:35:01,140 --> 00:35:06,720
The extortionists had built 25 tamper-proof booby trap devices inside a refrigerator bomb.

445
00:35:06,721 --> 00:35:12,280
authorities decided it would be safer to destroy the 1100 pound bomb in place

446
00:35:12,281 --> 00:35:14,820
rather than risk trying to disarm it

447
00:35:14,821 --> 00:35:27,540
there is another disturbing development in the use of booby traps

448
00:35:27,541 --> 00:35:32,700
otherwise law-abiding citizens are using them to take the law into their own hands

449
00:35:32,701 --> 00:35:40,420
We see private citizens, store owners, setting up their own form of booby traps to protect themselves, their property.

450
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:46,680
So when the burglar breaks into the back of a store at night again, that shotgun is there to face him.

451
00:35:47,300 --> 00:35:48,940
Of course, that's illegal.

452
00:35:50,760 --> 00:35:54,200
A classic case occurred in 1990 in Denver, Colorado.

453
00:35:55,480 --> 00:36:01,400
A warehouse owner, tired of frequent break-ins, rigged a 12-gauge shotgun booby trap to a window.

454
00:36:02,080 --> 00:36:07,140
When a teenage burglar was killed, the businessman was tried and convicted of manslaughter.

455
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:09,560
